==Description== <!--T:3-->

<!--T:4-->
The [[Image:BIM_ExtrudeFace.svg|24px]] '''BIM ExtrudeFace''' command extrudes a face, creating a [[Part_Extrude|Part Extrude]] object. It was split out from [[Draft_Trimex|Draft Trimex]] into its own command, since face extrusion is a distinct operation from trimming or extending geometry. {{Version|26.3}}

==Usage== <!--T:5-->

<!--T:6-->
See also: [[Draft_Snap|Draft Snap]] and [[Draft_Constrain|Draft Constrain]].

<!--T:7-->
# It can be helpful to first change the [[Draft_SelectPlane|Draft working plane]] so that it is not coplanar with the face you want to extrude.
# Optionally select a single face or an object with a single face.
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:BIM_ExtrudeFace.svg|16px]] [[BIM_ExtrudeFace|BIM ExtrudeFace]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Modification → [[Image:BIM_ExtrudeFace.svg|16px]] ExtrudeFace}} option from the menu.
#* Use the keyboard shortcut: {{KEY|T}} then {{KEY|R}}.
# If you have not yet selected an object or a face: select an object with a single face in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# The {{MenuCommand|Extrude Face}} task panel opens. See [[#Options|Options]] for more information.
# To define the extrusion direction and distance do one of the following:
#* Pick a point in the [[3D_View|3D View]] that does not lie on the same plane as the face.
#* Make sure the pointer is on the correct side of the face in the [[3D_View|3D View]] and enter a {{MenuCommand|Distance}}.

==Options== <!--T:8-->

<!--T:9-->
* '''Distance''': the extrusion length. Can be entered numerically or set by moving the pointer in the 3D View.


